Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Isolate seven gateway and ACP symbolic-home fixtures

Opt these seven owning modules into authority_cwd_in_tmp. Their real
SessionAuthority fixtures use symbolic profile_id values default/p as homes;
late scoped config reads otherwise resolve them under the checkout. Keep
all lifecycle, admission, cancel, rearm and route assertions and parameters.
No production change, timeout, retry, scheduling or strict-guard change.

Proof (HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0, per-file canonical runner + distinct XML):
- Exact sync source 4a1e82c0fda5f683d0a449e30517c215d8db7d3c:
  whole files execute 9/12/3/2/2/1/4 = 33 cases, all behavior passes;
  ACP False has an additional strict checkout-home teardown error for p.
- Selected reported functions, all parameters retained: 23 passes, no errors.
- Controlled late real load_config_readonly after each body under p/default:
  33 behavior passes + 33 strict checkout-home errors before isolation;
  same replay after isolated cwd: 33 passes, zero errors. The original guard
  is unchanged. Temporary diagnostic plugin is not shipped.
- Exact-source isolated whole files without injection: 33 passes.
- Fresh main c9d83070c83f + these marks: 33 passes, no skipped cases.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks pass using PM test interpreter.

Boundaries: the replay proves late symbolic-home contamination deterministically,
not the historical schedule of each CI occurrence 89-95. Natural traced repeat
was quiet; historical CI has no writer stack. The strict guard exists on the
sync source, not fresh main; main-only green is not strict-guard proof.
Fresh open PR file inventory had no overlap with these seven paths.

Hermes-Card: t_0ff7bd040eb88d40
